# Typography

Typeface: **IBM Plex Sans** (via `design-system/fonts`). No other family.

SoT for sizes: `design-system/tokens/typography.css`. Align this rule to the
tokens — never invent a parallel scale.

## Text roles

| Role | Usage | Token |
|---|---|---|
| Display | Page titles | `--text-display`, bold |
| Heading | Panel titles | `--text-heading`, bold |
| Body | Content | `--text-body` |
| Label | Meta, compact chrome | `--text-label` |
| Meta / eyebrow | Uppercase eyebrows, quiet facts | `--text-meta`, letter-spacing +0.06em when eyebrow |

## Numeric roles (identity carriers)

All product numbers use **tabular figures** (`.ds-num`:
`font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`).

| Role | Class / token | Where |
|---|---|---|
| Hero numeric | `.ds-num-hero` / `--text-hero-num` | Overview "Où en est-on ?", Match Hero score / kickoff |
| Score | `.ds-num-score` / `--text-score` | Large match scores |
| Row score | `.ds-num-row-score` / `--text-row-score` | MatchRow scores |
| Standings points | `.ds-num-pts` / `--text-standings-pts` | Pts column (dominates the row) |
| Counter | `.ds-num-counter` / `--text-counter` | À traiter counts, plateau occupancy |

Rules:
- A match score is always **bigger and bolder** than the team names around it.
- Points dominate a standings row; team name stays regular weight.
- Dates/times are body-size, secondary color — numbers dominate only when they
  are sport-meaningful (score, rank, points, matchday, plateau count).
